     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why does a heat pump blow warm air in cooling mode?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Warm air can reflect a thermostat setting, restricted airflow, a refrigerant problem, or a reversing valve that has not changed modes. City & Suburban repairs all makes and models. A service request should include whether the problem began after a mode change or developed during steady summer operation."
